xceptional so here we have vladislav  from the left who was the VFX artist  that we have miko working on music and  he and Martin who is next to me on the  right they were basically the magicians  who kind of figured out how to handle  that song in a way that adapts to what  the players doing at the player stop the  music and just works with that most  people program they even realize it how  complex that is to make it sound natural  but it kind of just  works and these two guys were behind  that then this anna-marie she is the  level designer basically responsible or  figuring the flow out and and kind of  taking all the different bits and pieces  making them come together and a lot of  the orchestration of the different  events that's by her as well she also  did many of the simple floor animations  and so on so she was essential to put  all of these different things together  then we have Marcel who's the  environment artist and then Leonardo his  concept artist so Leonardo early on  basically put those images together to  kind of illustrate the overall aesthetic  the sense of the you know the vertical  elements the symmetry tone that the  motel brings to the environment and all  of that stuff and then Marcel is the  environmentalist and Leonardo and Mossad  together worked a lot to figure all this  different bits together and must have  basically responsible of actually  implementing it I think the maze overall  is it's a successful exercise from  aesthetic perspective as well because I  do think that if you would show even a  small bed of this environment to anybody  who's played they immediately know like  yes that's the maze and can be a tiny  detail or a bigger thing the art  director Jana Paul keener together with  the VFX team then Marmont others did a  fantastic job it's Ted McDonald as well  who was the world design director the  person who kind of came up with all  these little details have different  things work the doors that shoes all of  the stuff again a lot of people come  together creating something unique the  the popularity of the Masons reception  to me surprised us a bit and to be  honest I'm not sure why because we  should have known already but still  we've kind of caught off guard a bit but  it kind of verified to us that what  we're doing as an independent small  studio it's important that we stick the  things that belongs to us and kind of  all things that only we are doing out  there and believe in that and not kind  of make the mistake of shying away from  something that might be a bit strange or  a bit  you whimsical and so on and instead be  ready to embrace that and trust that and  players will always get it they will  always have fun they will always  appreciate when we're doing something  different that is refreshing and fun and  unpure in in many ways and it kind of  got reaffirmed I think in a way that yes  that's the case and I think it will act  as guidance for us in the future as well  stick to our guns and and be who we are  and not shy away from that
 

